Assume POSIX semantics, that every call succeeds, and that file `x` exists. A process runs:

```c
int a = open("x", O_RDONLY);
int b = dup(a);
int c = open("x", O_RDONLY);
if (fork() == 0) {          // child
    close(a);
    int d = open("x", O_RDONLY);
    int e = dup(c);
    pause();
}
close(c);
pause();
```

When both processes are in `pause()`, how many **system-wide open-file-table entries** refer to `x`, and what is the **reference count** of the entry created by the first `open()`?

Assume POSIX semantics, that every call succeeds, that file `log` exists, and that no process exits before all reach `pause()`.

```c
int fd = open("log", O_RDONLY);
for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    if (fork() == 0)
        open("log", O_RDONLY);    // result discarded, never closed
    else if (i == 1)
        close(fd);
}
pause();
```

When every process is in `pause()`, what is the **total number of open file descriptors referring to `log`**, summed over all processes of this program (equivalently, the sum of the reference counts of all open-file-table entries for `log`)?

Assume orphans are adopted by init (PID 1), which promptly reaps them, no subreaper exists, and only sleep() takes significant time. Times are measured from the start of `main`.

```c
int main(void) {
    int i;
    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        if (fork() == 0 && i != 2)
            break;
    if (i < 3) {
        if (i == 1 && fork() == 0) {
            sleep(6);
            exit(0);
        }
        sleep(i + 1);
        exit(0);
    }
    wait(NULL);
    sleep(10);
    return 0;
}
```

How many processes created by this program are **zombies at t = 7**?

Assume orphans are adopted by `init` (PID 1), which promptly reaps its terminated children; no subreaper exists; only `sleep()` takes significant time. Times are measured from the start of `main`.

```c
int main(void) {               // P
    if (fork() == 0) {         // child C
        if (fork() == 0) {     // grandchild G
            sleep(5);
            exit(0);           // G exits at t ≈ 5
        }
        exit(0);               // C exits at t ≈ 0
    }
    sleep(10);
    wait(NULL);
    return 0;
}
```

