Assume orphans are adopted by `init` (PID 1), which promptly reaps its terminated children (including zombies it inherits); no subreaper exists; only `sleep()` takes significant time.

```c
int main(void) {                     // P
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        if (fork() == 0) {           // child i
            sleep(2 * i + 1);        // child i exits at t ≈ 2i + 1
            exit(0);
        }
    }
    sleep(4);
    return 0;                        // P exits at t ≈ 4
}
```

